argin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":-0.025289783334459,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.664274322169059,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.040128148503336195,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":46.7,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.0068276772369980305,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":6.8,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.047945022232382735,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":64.4,"_gate_share_shrink":0.009064983217221156,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":38.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.03510390833765884,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":41.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.00234,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Uber Technologies, Inc. develops and operates proprietary technology applications in the United States, Canada, Latin America, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia Pacific. The company operates through three segments: Mobility, Delivery, and Freight. The Mobility segment connects consumers with a range of transportation modalities, such as ridesharing, carsharing, micromobility, rentals, public transit, taxis, and other modalities; and offers riders in a variety of vehicle types, as well as financial partnerships products and advertising services. The Delivery segment allows consumers to search for and discover restaurants to grocery, alcohol, convenience, and other retailers, as well as order a meal or other items, and either pick-up at the restaurant or have it delivered; and provides Uber direct, a white-label delivery-as-a-service for retailers and restaurants, as well as advertising services. The Freight segment manages transportation and logistics networks, which connects shippers and carriers in digital marketplace, including carriers upfronts, pricing, and shipment booking; and offers on-demand platform to automate logistics end-to-end transactions for small-and medium-sized businesses to global enterprises. Uber Technologies, Inc. has strategic partnership with Mews to embed ride booking, real-time tracking and integrated billing directly into the Mews platform. The company was formerly known as Ubercab, Inc. and changed its name to Uber Technologies, Inc. in February 2011. Uber Technologies, Inc. was founded in 2009 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Dara  Khosrowshahi | CEO & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $4.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 37K people. Revenue per employee of $1.4M ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 24%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $262K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $49K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Uber Technologies, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $136.1B market cap on $52.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +18% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +11.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $9.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 19 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.00\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 13\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 4.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.5\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 85% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.84577402753175},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $186.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 9% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (52% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Sector under pressure with a 18.0% decline over the past 6 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Can Uber (NYSE:UBER) Extend Its Rally As Market Momentum Builds?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/technical-analysis/can-uber-nyseuber-extend-its-rally-as-market-momentum-builds","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795811400.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.513,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Uber Moves Closer To Delivery Hero Acquisition With 87% Stake","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/uber-moves-closer-delivery-hero-183636000.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795805000.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.995,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Uber Stock Is Moving Today","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/why-uber-stock-moving-today-180127291.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795802487.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Uber Moves Closer to Massive $14.8 Billion Takeover","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/uber-moves-closer-massive-14-141753945.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795789073.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Is UBER's Gross Bookings Strength a Catalyst for More Upside?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3036486/is-uber-s-gross-bookings-strength-a-catalyst-for-more-upside?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cquick_take-3036486","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795786500.0,"origin":"tiingo","